      "systemBoundaryDescription": [
        {
          "stage": "Rearing",
          "description": "During the rearing process, BSF are cultivated in climate-controlled environments with warm and humid conditions to create optimal settings for rapid growth. The larvae are fed with agricultural by-products and other side streams, which are considered waste materials. Therefore, according to the Module D principle in LCA, the environmental impacts of the feed are not attributed to this lifecycle of the BSF product. In addition, based on actual farm operations, water usage during the rearing phase is minimal and can be considered negligible. As a result, water consumption in this stage is not taken into account."
        },
        {
          "stage": "Production",
          "description": "At this stage, the BSF have been reared to the desired mature size to ensure optimal nutrient content and biomass. Subsequently, a series of necessary post-processing steps are carried out, including pre-drying and drying, to remove excess moisture and facilitate subsequent storage, transportation, and further processing. It should be noted that the final packaging of the product is not included in this stage."
        },
        {
          "stage": "Transportation",
          "description": "This stage includes the environmental impact of transporting the finished BSF protein products from production sites in China (CHN) to BSF Cycle distribution warehouses, accounting for both local and international logistics. The international segment involves maritime shipping from China to a port in Germany, followed by road transportation by truck from the German port to the BSF Cycle warehouse."
        }
